en't  seen Gurren Lagann why haven't you seen  it go watch it right now immediately and  then come right back  both Gurren Lagann and iron bladder  orphans begin in a place where the main  characters are essentially children who  are forced to do menial work and are  abused by their superiors but they take  their faith into their own hands and  form a powerful team Tiger and Don and  techadon respectively and this team then  faces off against much stronger  opponents and rivals and yet triumphs  against all odds on top of that  Miccosukee and Oregon have a similar  relationship to Simone and kameena but  whereas kameena needs to first teach  Simone to believe in the me who believes  in you Mika believes in orga 100% from  the get-go so much so that this makes  orga feel a great burden and great  responsibility because he blames himself  for all the suffering Mika puts himself  through for orga and the others there is  a really interesting and nuanced  friendship dynamic between Olga and Mika  and I really enjoy watching and develop  just like I enjoyed the dynamic between  Carmina and Simone  we'll say of course that iron blooded  orphans is not a perfect anime and it  does have some issues one of the issues  that I saw in the first season was that  Koo Dahlia seemed far too immature and  naive to me to be the leader of an  independence movement it just did not  seem to me like she was nearly mature  and strategic enough at that point to be  hailed as a hero of a sort of  independence movement or revolution I  also thought that in the second season  it was very naive for techadon to leave  the earth branch in the hands of rowdy  che and takaki Roddy Chi of course ends  up betraying them he is not part of  their inner circle and takaki who is  still a child has no sense of diplomacy  or leadership so he basically just  follows Roddy chair along blindly until  he is finally rescued by the rest of  techadon and he realizes that rod each  had betrayed them all and finally  towards the end of the second season I  found it very frustrating that both  McMurdo and NASA allowed that bastard  jazz Lee to work behind their backs and  keep stabbing him in the back over and  over again you would think that by this  time these guys would be capable enough  as leaders to see what's going on and to  deal with the threat so yeah those were  a few issues that I noticed with the  show that I personally was frustrated  with however those are minor in  comparison to all the great positives  that I've seen in this show  so in conclusion while I thought that  the action the music and other parts of  this anime were great the best thing  about iron blooded orphans in my opinion  was how maturely they deal with  important socio-economic issues how  realistically they portrayed the cruelty  of war and how they give us a really  nuanced and balanced view of human  nature so what did you think do you  agree with me what was your favorite  part about this anime let me know down  in the comments I would love to hear  from you as always thank you so much for  watching and be sure to subscribe and  hit that notification bell for more  videos like this one if you want to chat  about iron bladder orphans or any other  anime on a daily basis you can join our  discord server the link is in the  description and until next time see ya  space cowboys  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

